# Line endings the Linux guest depends on.
#
# The session scripts under tools/linuxfs/overlay are executed by bash inside the runtime.
# A CRLF checkout turns "set -u" into "set -u\r" and every function definition into a syntax
# error, so the session dies with exit status 2 before it prints anything (the 2026-10-01
# raw=2 launch failure). Windows checkouts run with core.autocrlf=true and this repository
# had no attributes file, so the working tree was CRLF while the blobs were LF - invisible
# to git status, fatal on the device.
#
tools/linuxfs/overlay/**        text eol=lf
app/src/main/assets/linuxfs/**  text eol=lf

# Anything else executed on the Linux side.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# gamescope patches are fed to `patch -p1` inside the Arch Linux ARM container. A CRLF patch
# file does not match the LF sources it patches; the blobs were already LF, so pin the
# checkout to match them instead of relying on the build host's git configuration.
*.patch text eol=lf

# This file drives the conversions above, so it must not be converted itself: with
# core.autocrlf=true a CRLF checkout would put a trailing CR into every pattern below.
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# The Windows side keeps its CRLF.
*.bat      text eol=crlf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
